If the pro-isomorphism $a$ is given by maps $a_ n : K_{m_ n} \to M_ n$ the we obtain a pro-isomorphism on $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits $ using the corresponding maps $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _\mathcal {D}(L, K_{m_ n}) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _\mathcal {D}(L, M_ n)$. Thus the construction of the arrows on $\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits $ and $R^1\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits $ in the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0H9K" data-tag="0H9K">15.88.4</a> agrees with the construction of $a'$ and $a''$ in Derived Categories, Remark <a href="/tag/0H9J" data-tag="0H9J">13.34.4</a>.